75120>>>// This provides a quick and simple way to create an about package for a program.
75120>>>// You need to create a message inside you client area called Activate_About.
75120>>>// Within this message you should send the message DoAbout passing needed
75120>>>// string information.
75120>>>//
75120>>>//       Procedure Activate_About
75120>>>//           Send DoAbout sTitle sVersion sCopyright sAuthor sBitmap
75120>>>//       End_Procedure
75120>>>//    where: sTitle =     Name of application. If none provided, uses caption
75120>>>//                        bar title
75120>>>//           sVersion   = Version Line. If none provided, will be blank
75120>>>//           sCopyRight = Copyright Line. If none provided, will be blank
75120>>>//           sAuthor    = Author name, blank if none provided
75120>>>//           sBitMap    = Bitmap logo. If none provided, standard VDF bitmap
75120>>>//                        is used.
75120>>>// It is expected that you will place this in your own object package. For
75120>>>// example an order about package may look like this:
75120>>>//
75120>>>//   // OrderAbout.pkg
75120>>>//   Use StdAbout.pkg
75120>>>//   Procedure Activate_About
75120>>>//      String sTitle sCopyright sVersion sAuthor
75120>>>//      Move "My Order Entry System" to sTitle
75120>>>//      Move "Version 2.1" to sVersion
75120>>>//      Move "Copyright xxxx, Super Software Inc." to sCopyright
75120>>>//      Move "John Smith"  to sAuthor
75120>>>//      Send DoAbout sTitle sVersion sCopyright sAuthor ""
75120>>>//   end_procedure
75120>>>//   // end of file.
